# What the analysis writes, which is a result and not a checked-in artifact.
#
# `pc test` runs every scenario of the knee gear's `fea:`, and
# `Shape.analyze_async()` writes the model each produced beside the package --
# `knee-gear.fea.dropped.glb`. The `Examples
# (PartCAD)` job then runs `pc render -r` and fails if anything under
# `examples/` changed; an untracked solver result is such a change. It is not
# checked in, for the reason `examples/feature_cae/.gitignore` gives: it is
# whatever the solver and the mesher produced on that machine, at those versions.
*.fea.glb
*.fea.*.glb
*.dynamic.glb
*.dynamic.*.glb
*.thermal.glb
*.thermal.*.glb
*.cfd.glb
*.cfd.*.glb
